.TH TARIA 1 "November 2026" "Taria 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
taria \- terminal-native Linux package manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B taria
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Taria provides a single command interface to installed native package managers and GitHub discovery. It delegates system package operations to APT/DPKG, Snap, or Pacman. It is a CLI tool and does not provide a GTK window.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B search, s QUERY
Search available local package sources and GitHub repositories.
.TP
.B install, i PACKAGE
Install a package. Administrator privileges are required.
.TP
.B remove, r PACKAGE
Remove a package. Use --purge for APT purge behavior.
.TP
.B info PACKAGE
Display package metadata.
.TP
.B list, ls
List installed packages.
.TP
.B update, u
Refresh package metadata. On Arch, perform a safe full sync and upgrade.
.TP
.B upgrade, up
Upgrade installed packages. Use --full for APT full-upgrade behavior.
.TP
.B doctor
Check supported package managers and the latest Taria GitHub release.
.TP
.B report MESSAGE
Search this project's public issue tracker for related messages. Local logs are not uploaded.
.TP
.B self-update
Check for or apply a checksum-verified Taria GitHub release. Applying an update requires sudo.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --source apt|snap|pacman|github|all
Select package source.
.TP
.B --purge
Use APT purge behavior when removing a package.
.TP
.B --full
Use the distribution's full-upgrade operation.
.TP
.B --check
Check for a Taria update without changing the installed executable.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
taria search firefox
sudo taria install firefox
sudo taria remove firefox
sudo taria update
sudo taria upgrade
taria doctor
sudo taria self-update
.fi
.SH SECURITY
Taria requires explicit sudo for system modifications. It does not silently elevate privileges and does not execute arbitrary GitHub repository source code. Self-updates require a matching SHA-256 checksum asset.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/taria/errors.log
Local error log.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/taria
Installed executable.
